 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the real property tax law, in relation to expanding the length\nof time to pay delinquent taxes in installments to thirty-six months",
    "basePrintNo": "S4585",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4585-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1184, RPT L",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Tax Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4585\n\nSPONSOR: SANDERS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the real property tax law, in relation\nto expanding the length of time to pay delinquent taxes in installments\nto thirty-six months\n\n \nPURPOSE:  This bill will effectively expand the length of time to pay\ndelinquent taxes in installments to thirty-six months.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill amends section 1184 of the real property tax law\nas it relates to increasing the maximum term of installment agreements\nfrom twenty-four months to thirty-six months.\n\nSection 2 of the bill relates to the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill provides people who fall behind on payments with the time to\nfully pay their delinquent taxes. As it currently stands, the twenty-\nfour month timeframe does not allow appropriate time for someone to\ncatch up on payments after enduring a temporary financial hardship. This\nbill relieves this problem by extending the length of time to pay delin-\nquent taxes by a calendar year. This legislation is optional for coun-\nties to adopt, and therefore non-intrusive to local governments.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nA.1542 of 2017-18,\nA.7446 of 2015-16\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
